<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>dev.tommoulard.pr-bot</string>

  <!-- brew bash 5.x: the script is 3.2-safe, but 5.x is what it is tested on -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/tommoulard/.claude/scripts/pr-bot.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!--
    Replaces dev.tommoulard.pr-sweep AND dev.tommoulard.ci-red-watch.  Install:

      launchctl bootout  gui/$UID/dev.tommoulard.pr-sweep
      launchctl bootout  gui/$UID/dev.tommoulard.ci-red-watch
      rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.tommoulard.{pr-sweep,ci-red-watch}.plist
      cp ~/.claude/scripts/dev.tommoulard.pr-bot.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.tommoulard.pr-bot.plist

    One interval, not two schedules: the CI half wants to run often, and the
    rebase half -- which force-pushes, and so cancels and re-runs a whole
    workflow every time -- opens only in the windows in $REBASE_WINDOWS inside
    the script (09:00 and 15:00).  Putting the window in the script rather than
    in a StartCalendarInterval is what lets a window survive a tick that never
    ran: the machine was asleep, or the previous tick still held the lock through
    a 45-minute fix session.  launchd would simply have dropped that sweep.
  -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>

  <!-- no burst at login; the first tick comes 30 minutes after load -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/tommoulard/.claude/logs/pr-bot/launchd.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/tommoulard/.claude/logs/pr-bot/launchd.err.log</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HOME</key><string>/Users/tommoulard</string>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/Users/tommoulard/.cargo/bin:/Users/tommoulard/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
